AC4-c102 L08 | True or false: the division with the largest residual income is the best performer. | False as a general rule. Residual income is an amount, so it depends on the size of the division. For two divisions with the same return on capital above the rate, the larger one has the larger residual income, because RI = (OI/C - r)C. Which division is bette
AC4-c113 L08 | In Lab 1, how do SIM-D and SIM-A compare on capital base and residual income? | SIM-D has the larger base, 124,000 cents against 59,000 for SIM-A, and the smaller residual income, -4130.00 against -2440.00 cents. SIM-D's return on its base is 5.67% against 4.86%, and both returns are below the rate, so both residual incomes are negative.
AC4-c114 L08 | In Lab 1, what are SIM-G's residual income and EVA? | Residual income of 2250.00 cents and EVA of -486.00 cents, so the two measures disagree in sign for SIM-G (Section 6).
AC4-c115 L08 | For the worked division, by how much does capitalizing an outlay of 100 SCU, with a first- | By 72.8 SCU, from 30 to 102.8 SCU (Section 4 and Proposition 8.4).
AC4-c116 L08 | For the worked division, by how much does capitalizing an outlay of 100 SCU, with a first- | By 56.8 SCU, from 6 to 62.8 SCU (Section 4 and Proposition 8.4).
AC4-c117 L07 | In the worked case, what is the lowest transfer price when supplier capacity is K = 12,000 | 44 SCU. With D falling to 1,000 units, the floor is 40 + 1,000 x 20 / 5,000 = 44 (Problem M2).
AC4-c129 L08 | In the Section 5 example, what residual income does division X have? | X has residual income of 15 SCU (C = 500, OI = 60, r = 9%).
AC4-c134 L08 | In the Section 5 example, what residual income does division Y have? | Y has residual income of 20 SCU (C = 2,000, OI = 200, r = 9%).
AC4-c091 L07 | Which transfer prices leave both divisions no worse off? | Exactly the prices t in the interval [t_min, t_max]. On that interval both gains are nonnegative, and outside it at least one gain is negative (Theorem 7.3, part 1).
